                    order: 1,
                    estimatedMinutes: 120,
                    theoryContent: "\r\n# Introduction to DevOps\r\n\r\n## What is DevOps?\r\n\r\nDevOps is a **cultural and technical movement** that emphasizes collaboration between development and operations teams to deliver software faster, more reliably, and with higher quality.\r\n\r\n### Key Points:\r\n- 🎯 **DevOps is NOT a tool** - it's a culture, methodology, and set of practices\r\n- 🔄 **Continuous Everything** - Integration, Delivery, Deployment, Monitoring\r\n- 🤝 **Breaking Silos** - Developers and Operations work together\r\n- 📈 **Faster Time to Market** - Reduce lead time from code commit to production\r\n- 🛡️ **Improved Reliability** - Automated testing and deployment reduce errors\r\n\r\n## The DevOps Lifecycle\r\n\r\n```\r\nPlan → Code → Build → Test → Release → Deploy → Operate → Monitor → Plan\r\n```\r\n\r\n### 1. **Plan** \r\n- Requirement gathering\r\n- Sprint planning\r\n- Work item tracking\r\n\r\n### 2. **Code**\r\n- Version control (Git)\r\n- Code review\r\n- Collaborative development\r\n\r\n### 3. **Build**\r\n- Compilation\r\n- Dependency management\r\n- Artifact creation\r\n\r\n### 4. **Test**\r\n- Unit testing\r\n- Integration testing\r\n- Security scanning\r\n\r\n### 5. **Release**\r\n- Release planning\r\n- Approval workflows\r\n- Release automation\r\n\r\n### 6. **Deploy**\r\n- Infrastructure provisioning\r\n- Application deployment\r\n- Configuration management\r\n\r\n### 7. **Operate**\r\n- Service management\r\n- Incident response\r\n- Performance optimization\r\n\r\n### 8. **Monitor**\r\n- Application monitoring\r\n- Infrastructure monitoring\r\n- Log aggregation\r\n- User analytics\r\n\r\n## DevOps vs Traditional IT\r\n\r\n| Aspect | Traditional IT | DevOps |\r\n|--------|---------------|---------|\r\n| Deployment | Manual, Monthly | Automated, Multiple times/day |\r\n| Teams | Siloed | Integrated |\r\n| Feedback | Slow | Continuous |\r\n| Testing | End of cycle | Throughout lifecycle |\r\n| Recovery | Hours/Days | Minutes |\r\n\r\n## Important Principles\r\n\r\n### 🔑 **The Three Ways of DevOps**\r\n\r\n1. **Flow** - Fast flow of work from Dev to Ops to customer\r\n2. **Feedback** - Continuous feedback loops at all stages\r\n3. **Continuous Learning** - Culture of experimentation and learning\r\n\r\n### 🎯 **CALMS Framework**\r\n\r\n- **C**ulture - Collaborative culture\r\n- **A**utomation - Automate repetitive tasks\r\n- **L**ean - Eliminate waste\r\n- **M**easurement - Measure everything\r\n- **S**haring - Share knowledge and responsibilities\r\n\r\n## Benefits of DevOps\r\n\r\n✅ **Speed** - Deploy features faster\r\n✅ **Reliability** - Fewer failures in production\r\n✅ **Scale** - Manage infrastructure at scale\r\n✅ **Security** - Integrated security practices\r\n✅ **Collaboration** - Better team dynamics\r\n✅ **Customer Satisfaction** - Faster feature delivery\r\n\r\n## Common DevOps Metrics\r\n\r\n- **Deployment Frequency** - How often you deploy\r\n- **Lead Time** - Time from commit to production\r\n- **Mean Time to Recovery (MTTR)** - Recovery time from failures\r\n- **Change Failure Rate** - Percentage of deployments causing failures\r\n\r\n## Key Takeaways\r\n\r\n> 💡 DevOps is about **people, process, and tools** - in that order!\r\n\r\n> 🚀 Start small, automate incrementally, measure continuously\r\n\r\n> 🤝 Foster a culture of trust, collaboration, and shared responsibility\r\n          ",
